From b768284d55ffb584511a9e4340c73a5adffab9d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 07:52:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] feat(logs): record error_code, http_status,
 correlation_id and provider job id
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

request_logs said only "Fail", with a free-text message that was often empty,
so the API Logs page could not answer any of the questions an operator
actually has: what kind of failure, what the upstream answered, which
container log lines belong to it, which provider job it was.

Revision 6d2e3f4a5b6c adds the four nullable columns (error_code,
correlation_id and provider_job_id indexed — they are what you search by).
log_usage — the single writer of this table — takes them, and defaults the
correlation id to the one already stamped on the current request's log lines.

The chat turn carries its classification through TurnOutcome, and the video
worker now runs inside `correlation_scope(job_id)`, so every line it logs
carries the job id and the request-log row points back at exactly those
lines. A failed video also records the OpenRouter job id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
